<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Configuration Drift Assessment — {{ org_name }}</title>
<style>
/* Everything is inline. No CDN, no external font, no remote image.
   The report has to survive being attached to a change ticket and opened
   offline months later. */
:root {
  --ink: #14181f; --muted: #5b6472; --line: #e2e6ec; --bg: #ffffff; --panel: #f7f8fa;
  --critical: #a4161a; --critical-bg: #fdf0f0;
  --high: #bc4b00; --high-bg: #fdf4ec;
  --medium: #8a6d00; --medium-bg: #fcf8e8;
  --low: #2f6b45; --low-bg: #eff6f1;
  --info: #3a5a8c; --info-bg: #eef3fa;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0; padding: 0 0 80px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
.wrap { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px; }
header.cover { border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink); padding: 56px 0 28px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
.eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 12px; }
h1 { font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
.subtitle { font-size: 17px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 24px; }
.meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 40px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.meta div { margin-bottom: 4px; }
.meta strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.demo-banner {
  background: var(--info-bg); border: 1px solid #c6d5ea; border-left: 4px solid var(--info);
  padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; margin: 24px 0 0; color: #24406b;
}
h2 {
  font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 8px; margin: 48px 0 20px;
}
h3 { font-size: 17px; margin: 28px 0 8px; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
.verdict { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 24px; font-size: 15.5px; }
.verdict p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
.verdict p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.scores { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 20px; }
.score { flex: 1 1 120px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 16px; background: #fff; }
.score .n { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
.score .l { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 6px; }
{% for s in ['critical','high','medium','low'] %}
.score.{{ s }} { background: var(--{{ s }}-bg); }
.score.{{ s }} .n { color: var(--{{ s }}); }
.pill.{{ s }} { background: var(--{{ s }}); color: #fff; }
.finding.{{ s }} { border-left: 5px solid var(--{{ s }}); }
td.cell.{{ s }} { background: var(--{{ s }}-bg); color: var(--{{ s }}); font-weight: 700; }
{% endfor %}
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13.5px; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
th { text-align: left; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }
td { padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
td.cell { text-align: center; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
.mono { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12px; }
.tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--muted); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 5px; margin-right: 3px; }
.pill { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
.pill.info { background: var(--info); color: #fff; }
.finding { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 20px 24px; margin: 0 0 16px; background: #fff; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.finding-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.finding-head .id { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; }
.finding h3 { margin: 6px 0 2px; font-size: 16.5px; }
.finding .where { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
.block { margin: 14px 0 0; }
.block .label { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 4px; }
.block p { margin: 0; }
.block.evidence p { background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px; padding: 10px 12px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: #33404f; word-break: break-word; }
.roadmap-phase { margin-bottom: 24px; }
.roadmap-phase .phase-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.roadmap-phase h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; }
.roadmap-phase .when { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
ol.actions { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
ol.actions li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
ol.actions .who { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
ul.plain { margin: 8px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
ul.plain li { margin-bottom: 7px; }
.method-grid { display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.method-col { flex: 1 1 280px; }
footer { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
.empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; padding: 12px 0; }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
.bar { display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; width: 70px; height: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--line); overflow: hidden; margin-right: 6px; }
.bar span { display: block; height: 100%; }
.bar span.critical { background: var(--critical); }
.bar span.medium { background: var(--medium); }
.bar span.low { background: var(--low); }
@media print {
  body { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0 12mm; }
  .finding, .roadmap-phase, table { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { page-break-after: avoid; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="cover">
  <p class="eyebrow">Network Assessment</p>
  <h1>Configuration Drift Assessment</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">{{ org_name }} &mdash; Cisco Meraki organization</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <div><strong>Source</strong><br>{{ source }}</div>
    <div><strong>Baseline</strong><br>{{ baseline.name }} &middot; v{{ baseline.version }}</div>
    <div><strong>Assessment date</strong><br>{{ generated_at }}</div>
    <div><strong>Access level</strong><br>Read-only (GET only)</div>
    <div><strong>Networks / devices</strong><br>{{ site_matrix|length }} / {{ inventory|length }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if demo %}
  <div class="demo-banner">
    <strong>Demonstration report.</strong> Generated from bundled fixture data
    representing a fictional three-site company. No Meraki organization was
    contacted. Every name, serial, address and identifier in this document is synthetic.
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</header>

<!-- 1 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>1 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Executive summary</h2>

<div class="scores">
  {% for severity in ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] %}
  <div class="score {{ severity }}"><div class="n">{{ counts[severity] }}</div><div class="l">{{ severity }}</div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="score"><div class="n">{{ site_matrix|length }}</div><div class="l">Networks</div></div>
</div>

<div class="verdict">
  {% for paragraph in verdict %}<p>{{ paragraph }}</p>{% endfor %}
</div>

{% if counts['critical'] %}
<h3>Breaking something now</h3>
<ul class="plain">
  {% for finding in findings if finding.severity == 'critical' %}
  <li><strong>{{ finding.target }}</strong> &mdash; {{ finding.finding }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

<!-- 2 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>2 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Sites at a glance</h2>

<p>Findings per network and area. Cell colour is the most severe finding in that cell.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Network</th>
      <th class="num">Devices</th>
      {% for key, label in category_labels.items() %}<th style="text-align:center" title="{{ label }}">{{ category_short.get(key, label) }}</th>{% endfor %}
      <th class="num">Total</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in site_matrix %}
    <tr>
      <td style="white-space:nowrap"><strong>{{ row.name }}</strong>{% if row.tags %}<br>{% for t in row.tags %}<span class="tag">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.devices }}</td>
      {% for key, cell in row.cells.items() %}
      <td class="cell {{ cell.worst }}">{{ cell.count if cell.count else '—' }}</td>
      {% endfor %}
      <td class="num"><strong>{{ row.total }}</strong></td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Device inventory <span class="mono">({{ inventory|length }})</span></h3>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Network</th><th>Device</th><th>Model</th><th>Serial</th><th>Firmware</th><th>LAN IP</th><th class="num">Findings</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for item in inventory %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ item.network }}</td>
      <td><strong>{{ item.name }}</strong></td>
      <td>{{ item.model }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ item.serial }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ item.firmware }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ item.lan_ip or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ item.finding_count or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{% if address_space %}
<h3>Address space <span class="mono">({{ address_space|length }} VLANs)</span></h3>
<p>Each VLAN's DHCP pool after reserved ranges, fixed reservations and the
appliance IP are removed, against distinct addresses seen in use by clients in
the last 7 days. Observed use over a week is an upper bound on concurrent
leases, so utilisation here errs high.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Network</th><th>VLAN</th><th>Subnet</th><th>DHCP</th><th class="num">Reserved</th><th class="num">Fixed</th><th class="num">Pool</th><th class="num">In use</th><th style="min-width:120px">Utilisation</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for r in address_space %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.network }}</td>
      <td><strong>{{ r.vlan }}</strong> {{ r.name }}</td>
      <td class="mono">{{ r.subnet }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'MX' if r.dhcp == 'Run a DHCP server' else ('relay' if 'Relay' in r.dhcp else r.dhcp) }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.reserved or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.fixed or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.pool if r.pool is not none else '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.in_use }}</td>
      <td>
        {% if r.utilisation is not none %}
        {% set pct = (r.utilisation * 100)|round|int %}
        {% set tone = 'critical' if pct >= 90 else ('medium' if pct >= 80 else 'low') %}
        <div class="bar"><span class="{{ tone }}" style="width: {{ [pct, 100]|min }}%"></span></div>
        <span class="mono">{{ pct }}%</span>
        {% else %}<span class="mono">n/a</span>{% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if nac_posture %}
<h3>802.1X posture <span class="mono">({{ nac_posture|length }} switches)</span></h3>
<p>Enabled access ports by enforcement, and how wired clients seen in the last
7 days were admitted. A client on an enforcing port with an 802.1X identity
authenticated; one without came in through MAB; one in the policy's guest or
failed-auth VLAN failed.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Network</th><th>Switch</th><th class="num">Access ports</th><th class="num">Enforcing</th><th class="num">Exempt</th><th class="num">Open</th><th class="num">802.1X</th><th class="num">MAB</th><th class="num">Failed</th><th class="num">On open ports</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for r in nac_posture %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.network }}</td>
      <td><strong>{{ r.switch }}</strong></td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.access_ports }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.enforcing or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.exempt or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num {{ 'cell high' if r.open else '' }}">{{ r.open or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.dot1x or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.mab or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num {{ 'cell medium' if r.failed else '' }}">{{ r.failed or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.on_open or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- 3 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>3 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Findings</h2>

{% if not findings %}<p class="empty">No drift from the baseline.</p>{% endif %}

{% for finding in findings %}
<div class="finding {{ finding.severity }}">
  <div class="finding-head">
    <span class="pill {{ finding.severity }}">{{ finding.severity }}</span>
    <span class="id">DRIFT-{{ '%03d' % loop.index }}</span>
    <span class="id">{{ finding.category_label }}</span>
  </div>
  <h3>{{ finding.finding }}</h3>
  <div class="where">{{ finding.target }}</div>
  <div class="block evidence"><div class="label">Evidence</div><p>{{ finding.evidence }}</p></div>
  <div class="block"><div class="label">Business risk</div><p>{{ finding.risk }}</p></div>
  <div class="block"><div class="label">Remediation</div><p>{{ finding.remediation }}</p></div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<!-- 4 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>4 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Remediation roadmap</h2>

<p>Sequenced by consequence, not by effort. The first phase is service restoration
and belongs in the next change window.</p>

{% for phase in roadmap %}
<div class="roadmap-phase">
  <div class="phase-head">
    <span class="pill {{ phase.severity }}">{{ phase.severity }}</span>
    <h3>{{ phase.title }}</h3>
    <span class="when">{{ phase.timeframe }}</span>
  </div>
  <ol class="actions">
    {% for action in phase.actions %}<li>{{ action.summary }}<br><span class="who">{{ action.detail }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
  </ol>
</div>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No remediation actions required.</p>
{% endfor %}

<h3>Structural recommendations</h3>
<ul class="plain">
  <li><strong>Gate network changes on this comparison.</strong> Every finding above
      was detectable from configuration alone. Running the audit as the last step
      of a cutover or hardware swap, before the change is closed, turns a week-long
      silent outage into a five-minute fix.</li>
  <li><strong>Keep the standard in version control.</strong> The baseline used here
      is a reviewed YAML file. When the standard changes, the change is a pull
      request with a reason, and "when did we start requiring VLAN 40 on uplinks?"
      has an answer.</li>
  <li><strong>Tag uplinks in Dashboard.</strong> Port tags make intent machine-readable.
      An uplink tagged <span class="mono">uplink</span> can be checked automatically;
      one identified only by its cable label cannot.</li>
  <li><strong>Give temporary changes an expiry.</strong> "TEMP" rules and installer
      SSIDs persist because nothing forces anyone to remove them. A comment with a
      date and an owner, and a recurring audit that flags it, does.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 5 ------------------------------------------------------------------ -->
<h2>5 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Methodology, scope and limitations</h2>

<div class="method-grid">
  <div class="method-col"><h3>What was examined</h3><ul class="plain">{% for item in scope_covered %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
  <div class="method-col"><h3>What was not examined</h3><ul class="plain">{% for item in scope_excluded %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
</div>

<h3>Access and method</h3>
<p>
  Configuration was read through the Meraki Dashboard API using HTTP GET requests
  only. No create, update or delete operation exists anywhere in the tool's
  codebase, and its CI pipeline fails the build if one is added. No configuration
  was changed, no device was rebooted, and no traffic was generated on the
  audited networks. Findings are a comparison between live configuration and the
  baseline <span class="mono">{{ baseline.source }}</span> (v{{ baseline.version }}).
</p>

<h3>Severity definitions</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Severity</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for severity in ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] %}
    <tr><td><span class="pill {{ severity }}">{{ severity }}</span></td><td>{{ severity_definitions[severity] }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Limitations</h3>
<ul class="plain">
  <li><strong>Drift is measured against the baseline, not against best practice.</strong>
      A network that matches a weak baseline will report clean. The baseline is
      included with this report so it can be reviewed on its own merits.</li>
  <li><strong>Uplinks are identified by port tag or name.</strong> An uplink that is
      neither tagged nor named as one is not assessed, and is listed below if trunk
      ports were seen without an identifiable uplink.</li>
  <li><strong>Firewall shadowing is computed structurally.</strong> CIDR containment is
      evaluated exactly; VLAN object references and FQDNs are compared by equality,
      so overlap between differently-expressed objects can be missed.</li>
  {% for limitation in scope_limitations %}<li>{{ limitation }}</li>{% endfor %}
  <li><strong>Point-in-time.</strong> This reflects configuration as of {{ generated_at }}.</li>
</ul>

<footer>
  Generated by <strong>meraki-config-auditor</strong> v{{ version }} &mdash; read-only
  Meraki configuration drift assessment.<br>
  {{ generated_at }}{% if demo %} &middot; demonstration data{% endif %}
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
